# vim spell checker

## What does this do:

Vim's built-in spell checker. Misspelled words are highlighted (red underline
on this system). Custom word list lives at ~/.vim/spell/en.utf-8.add.

## Navigating misspelled words

# Jump to next misspelled word
]s

# Jump to previous misspelled word
[s

# Jump to next misspelled word (bad words only, skip rare/region words)
]S

## Fixing misspelled words

# Show numbered suggestion list — type a number + Enter to accept
z=

# Accept the top suggestion instantly (no menu)
1z=

# Accept Nth suggestion instantly
2z=

## Managing the custom word list

# Mark word under cursor as correct (adds to ~/.vim/spell/en.utf-8.add)
zg

# Mark word under cursor as wrong (adds to bad-words list)
zw

# Undo zg — remove word from good list
zug

# Undo zw — remove word from bad list
zuw

## Toggling spell check on/off

# Enable spell checking
:set spell

# Disable spell checking
:set nospell

# Toggle
:set spell!

## Changing language

# Switch to British English
:set spelllang=en_gb

# Check multiple languages at once
:set spelllang=en_us,en_gb

# Check against all installed languages
:set spelllang=en

## Viewing full help

:help spell
